1
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:06,040
Taming The Husband

2
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:08,520
Episode 14

3
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,560
The Xie Estate

4
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:22,480
What's wrong?

5
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:26,440
By the pond, you asked
if we could look out for each other.

6
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,600
I had nothing to promise you then.

7
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:29,880
Now I do.

8
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:31,200
I've got a good job for you.

9
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:32,520
Don't feel you have to.

10
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:34,960
I heard the salt shop's doing very well,

11
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:36,720
but staffing it alone
must cost you a fortune.

12
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:41,600
Is hiring me really a good idea?

13
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:42,920
Why wouldn't it be?

14
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,120
You helped me, so I should help you, too.

15
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:46,840
But remember, you owe me one.

16
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:49,320
When you get ahead, look out for me.

17
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:52,960
Of all the times to come, he picks now!

18
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:55,360
What did you say?

19
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:59,440
I said,
I only know how to work with herbs,

20
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:00,680
yet you put so much faith in me.

21
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:02,600
Of course!

22
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:05,520
I heard Aunt Shen
run these shops for years

23
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:08,280
and since you grew up with her,
you must know more than I do.

24
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:14,400
If we're trapped in a tiny space,

25
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:17,400
let's swim fast
and leap through the Dragon Gate!

26
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:33,080
You--

27
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:36,280
What?

28
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:38,600
Trying to murder your husband?

29
00:02:39,240 --> 00:02:41,680
Why aren't you asleep in your own room?
What are you doing here?

30
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:44,520
Why aren't you asleep?
Where have you been this late?

31
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:46,920
Me? Recruiting my troops.

32
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:52,360
I suppose
it's the man you bought noodles for.

33
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:54,360
Why not say the man who healed your legs?

34
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:56,600
I don't care who he is. He's a man.

35
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,440
It's the middle of the night!

36
00:02:58,520 --> 00:02:59,840
Haven't you heard of propriety?

37
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:07,120
Look! Look what you've done to me!

38
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:10,800
Let me see.

39
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:12,760
You've always had a temper.

40
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:15,040
Besides, I never went into his room.

41
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,920
There was a thick wall between us!

42
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:25,040
Someone saw you
touching a man's hand by the lake!

43
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:26,680
Is it true?

44
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:29,360
His legs had gone numb,
so I helped him up.

45
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,800
So you did touch him!

46
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:33,240
Stop pretending to be so proper!

47
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:34,800
If you weren't tensing up on purpose,

48
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:35,960
why would it be so hard?

49
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:37,440
You look good enough to eat, too.

50
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:39,640
Don't try that on me!

51
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:42,080
Just because you know a few fancy words
doesn't mean you can throw them around!

52
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:44,320
I'll help you find someone,

53
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:45,440
but it can't be him!

54
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:47,960
But he knows about the salt shop the most.

55
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:50,000
After all he's done for us,
if we can't get him that letter,

56
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:51,240
can't we at least give him a job?

57
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:53,400
He's had plenty of reward money!

58
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:56,080
All that money has already gone
into your uncle's pocket!

59
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:58,520
Do you know how much he suffered
to treat your legs?

60
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:00,640
If he could heal my legs,

61
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:02,440
why can't he heal his own face?

62
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Xie Yan!

63
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:05,480
Can you stop
making those nasty little remarks?

64
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:06,800
Let me tell you, you're really annoying!

65
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:08,240
We're husband and wife!

66
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,920
Can't I even ask what you're doing?

67
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:13,800
Husband and wife?

68
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:15,200
Do you know what that means?

69
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,800
People who love each other!

70
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:18,440
And you? Why did you marry me?

71
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:20,560
Someone else didn't want you,
so you married me!

72
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:22,240
And you call us husband and wife?

73
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:23,520
Listen, Xie Yan,

74
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,200
all I owe you is money

75
00:04:25,280 --> 00:04:27,720
and three years gives me plenty of time
to pay it back bit by bit.

76
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:29,680
Why do you have to stick your nose
into everything?

77
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:35,160
Fine!

78
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:36,640
Jin Baozhu!

79
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:39,520
I don't want it

80
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:41,840
since you don't want me anyway!

81
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:45,320
I don't care for your things!

82
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:57,000
Baozhu.

83
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:04,480
I made this for you.

84
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:36,840
Throw it away, then!

85
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:39,000
You've been able to walk for ages!

86
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:47,520
You can go to anyone you like!

87
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:51,080
I can't get up.

88
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:55,240
Will you help me back?

89
00:05:57,280 --> 00:06:00,440
I can do this
without your permission, too.

90
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:04,000
And if you can stand up now,

91
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:06,160
why can't I?

92
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:25,040
-Young Master Xie!
-Young Master Xie!

93
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:27,360
Young Master Xie!

94
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:29,600
Good work.

95
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:31,360
Take your time, my lord.

96
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:33,320
-Careful.
-All right.

97
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:36,800
My lord, are you all right?

98
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:39,680
-Young Master Xie!
-Young Master Xie!

99
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:40,880
I'm the new steward.

100
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:42,000
I'm the new accountant.

101
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:46,160
Xie Salt Shop, licensed well salt

102
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:47,560
One at a time!

103
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:49,400
Here, form a line! One at a time!

104
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:50,960
Here.

105
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:54,240
Line up, everyone! Keep the doorway clear!

106
00:06:54,320 --> 00:06:56,520
Licensed well salt

107
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:57,720
Here. Yours.

108
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:00,240
All right, all right. Coming!

109
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:02,760
This is yours.

110
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,680
Salt permits issued. Payments received.

111
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:58,200
Since you've come all the way here,
why not go in and say hello?

112
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:01,000
I was just passing by,

113
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:04,680
so there's no need to say hello.

114
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:07,120
Such charming company.

115
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:09,600
-My lord!
-Why spoil their fun?

116
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:12,080
-My lord!
-What?

117
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:13,800
It hurts!

118
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:16,320
It hurts!

119
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:24,400
Let's go.

120
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:25,760
Come here.

121
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:28,800
Look at this.

122
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:34,320
My lord, stop watching.

123
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:35,480
Let's go home, my lord.

124
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:39,440
She's worked up such a sweat,

125
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,720
but hasn't even stopped for water.

126
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:42,920
What an idiot.

127
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:48,320
Where did she learn all those moves?

128
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:51,800
She's quite good at it.

129
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:55,040
You're not angry anymore?

130
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:56,760
Why would I be angry?

131
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:03,360
I'm just thinking,

132
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:06,120
when has she ever been this happy at home?

133
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:09,760
Lady Jin responds to kindness, not force.

134
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:13,560
I couldn't see that

135
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:15,840
because I was too worried
to think straight.

136
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:17,680
What was that?

137
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:21,800
I said, a fish belongs in open water.

138
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:23,480
Let her swim.

139
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:26,640
I'm her husband.

140
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:29,680
Why would her being friendly
with someone make me…

141
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:31,440
Make me angry? Right?

142
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:33,000
-Right?
-Of course.

143
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:34,080
Yes.

144
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:35,840
Let's go.

145
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,000
I'm fine.

146
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:49,880
Well?

147
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,680
Dazzling, isn't it?

148
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:57,760
Let's see what you've got to say now!

149
00:09:58,720 --> 00:10:00,280
What did you call me before?

150
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:01,400
A monkey in a hat?

151
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:02,720
A monkey in finery.

152
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:05,240
-Idiot!
-You dare say it again!

153
00:10:05,760 --> 00:10:08,880
I earned this private allowance myself!

154
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:11,480
Take that! Be jealous!

155
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:21,800
If you've earned money,

156
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:23,680
why not pay off your debt

157
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:25,960
so I can set you free sooner?

158
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:30,480
I…

159
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:34,160
Of course I'll enjoy a little of it first,

160
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:35,960
wear gold and silver,

161
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:37,520
and clash red with green!

162
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:39,520
I'll be as gaudy as I like,
and keep you waiting as long as I can!

163
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:41,000
What's the hurry?

164
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:56,760
I'm happy for you.

165
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,000
You…

166
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:01,920
How can you do that?

167
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,040
That's against the rules!

168
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,680
What rules?

169
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:08,440
It's supposed to be one insult from me,
one from you!

170
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:11,320
Now when I insult you,
you smile at me instead

171
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:13,080
and make me look like a complete jerk!

172
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:17,040
You're not a jerk.

173
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:19,120
You're amazing.

174
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:28,520
I was wrong.

175
00:11:29,840 --> 00:11:31,080
I was afraid you'd get hurt,

176
00:11:31,640 --> 00:11:32,880
so I tried to do everything for you.

177
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:35,680
I'm sorry.

178
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:38,800
I know what you want now.

179
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:41,040
I won't stand in your way.

180
00:11:42,680 --> 00:11:45,240
Let's stop fighting, all right?

181
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:50,200
From now on,

182
00:11:51,040 --> 00:11:52,640
if there's anything I can do,

183
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:54,200
just let me know,

184
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,040
because I want to help.

185
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:05,480
Now,

186
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:10,400
do you still want me?

187
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:18,280
I was angry, too

188
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:19,880
and said things I shouldn't have,

189
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:21,520
so I'm sorry, too.

190
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:26,000
But promise me, no more breaking things.

191
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:32,440
I promise.

192
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:40,280
And keep the day after tomorrow free.

193
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:43,640
I've invited our siblings and cousins
to dinner in the courtyard.

194
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:44,880
What's the occasion?

195
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:48,560
Fifth month, day 28, your birthday.

196
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:53,880
-If you don't want to--
-I do!

197
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:55,480
I've never celebrated my birthday.

198
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:03,960
Then I'll celebrate it for you.

199
00:13:23,920 --> 00:13:25,560
This should be fun! I'm going.

200
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:31,000
I won't join in,

201
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:32,880
so I don't spoil your fun.

202
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:34,480
Invitation

203
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:37,040
I'm going.

204
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:39,280
I've got something to tell your lady.

205
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:42,040
My lord.

206
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:44,800
Is he coming?

207
00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:47,040
The invitation's been delivered,
but there's no reply yet.

208
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,600
When he was treating my legs,

209
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:51,960
I never thought of it that way.

210
00:13:52,040 --> 00:13:54,960
Baozhu's birthday, Lunar May 28,
Xie Yan invites Song Jingxing

211
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:56,440
Things are different now.

212
00:13:59,280 --> 00:14:00,560
I'd like to meet him properly.

213
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:14,040
Jin Baozhu!

214
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:16,160
Jin Baozhu, come out!

215
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:17,320
I want to talk to you!

216
00:14:18,880 --> 00:14:20,480
What can't you say here?

217
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:22,600
Are you afraid of me?

218
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:28,440
As for the divination blocks
and plum drink,

219
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:29,840
my mother didn't tamper with either.

220
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:32,440
The Cowherd denied
taking the Weaver Girl's clothes, too.

221
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:34,160
Don't go!

222
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:37,200
It hurts!

223
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:38,480
It hurts!

224
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:39,560
Jin Baozhu,

225
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:40,720
I've tried to get you a few times.

226
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:42,320
You know all my tricks!

227
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:44,760
If I could plan anything that carefully,

228
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:46,320
you'd have been gone long ago!

229
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:47,400
Who else could it be?

230
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:49,160
Zhou Wanjun.

231
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:51,000
The lady of the house framed us!

232
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:53,840
Think about it. Who gave my mother

233
00:14:53,920 --> 00:14:55,200
that prescription for Yan?

234
00:14:55,280 --> 00:14:56,440
She did!

235
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:59,360
Do you have proof?

236
00:14:59,920 --> 00:15:00,920
No.

237
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:03,400
She's far too careful for that.

238
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:04,640
Then why would she do it?

239
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:06,800
I… How should I know?

240
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:10,760
So you're telling me this
to get me to bring her down for you?

241
00:15:10,840 --> 00:15:12,280
Do you think I'm stupid?

242
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:13,840
It's the truth!

243
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:16,440
-Really! I swear!
-Stop swearing!

244
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:18,400
If every oath in this world were true,

245
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:19,520
we'd be deaf from all the thunder!

246
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:22,200
Why won't you believe me?

247
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:24,040
You hate me so much, why invite me here?

248
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:25,880
And why break that teacup for me?

249
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:30,640
I admit, with the Huangs,

250
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:32,000
I dragged you into it on purpose.

251
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:35,200
I invited you today to make it up to you.

252
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:37,960
I'm petty and hotheaded,

253
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:39,160
and I can't separate one thing
from another.

254
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:41,000
I'm biased against you

255
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:42,440
and one meal won't change that.

256
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:44,640
If you accept it, stay.

257
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:46,520
If not, go.

258
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:49,000
Jin Baozhu!

259
00:15:58,360 --> 00:15:59,360
I got you

260
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:00,920
this compass,

261
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:03,800
so now we're even.

262
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:05,160
I'll eat you out of house and home!

263
00:16:12,040 --> 00:16:13,360
How's the food coming along?

264
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:14,720
-Almost.
-Just put it here.

265
00:16:15,640 --> 00:16:17,560
Baozhu!

266
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:20,160
-Happy birthday!
-Thank you!

267
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:21,640
Pour us plenty of wine later!

268
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:28,440
May joy and gladness fill your days.

269
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:29,520
Thank you.

270
00:16:30,320 --> 00:16:32,120
-Here.
-Happy birthday, Baozhu.

271
00:16:32,680 --> 00:16:33,680
That's thoughtful.

272
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:35,880
Beautiful!

273
00:16:36,640 --> 00:16:37,960
From Qiao.

274
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:40,120
A happy birthday, peace, and good health.

275
00:16:41,480 --> 00:16:42,840
Not bad!

276
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:47,800
Mr. Song's here, too.

277
00:16:50,720 --> 00:16:52,800
Your flowers are pretty,

278
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:54,640
but why do they look so dejected?

279
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:57,400
Young Master Yi,
they're dyed with garden balsam

280
00:16:57,480 --> 00:16:58,760
and called Trailing Jasmine.

281
00:16:58,840 --> 00:17:00,920
Trailing Jasmine,
a beauty who bows her head

282
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,000
rather than compete with other blooms.

283
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:03,880
What makes you think

284
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:05,320
we're trying to compete with you?

285
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:07,880
Stop it. I like them all.

286
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:09,920
Sit down.

287
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:14,160
Put it here.

288
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:18,480
-Excuse me!
-What are you doing?

289
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:21,040
My lord says these flowers
don't match the others,

290
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:22,440
-so he wants them kept in his room.
-This dish is pretty good.

291
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:31,320
Baozhu, why hasn't Yan come out yet?

292
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:33,640
-Xie Yan!
-Yan!

293
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:56,200
Look at that peacock strut!

294
00:17:56,760 --> 00:17:57,760
What's got into him?

295
00:17:58,320 --> 00:17:59,640
Must be rain on the way.

296
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,200
Congratulations!

297
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:16,600
Congratulations!

298
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,560
General Store

299
00:18:31,640 --> 00:18:32,840
But it's not raining.

300
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:34,920
Sorry to keep you waiting, everyone.

301
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:37,120
Yan, sit.

302
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:45,960
Move over.

303
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:55,280
What? You have something to tell me?

304
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:00,600
I do have a few words to say.

305
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:04,160
This first cup is to all of you,

306
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:05,640
and to me.

307
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:06,720
It's my birthday feast

308
00:19:06,800 --> 00:19:07,840
and I'm grateful you all came.

309
00:19:07,920 --> 00:19:09,160
If I've caused you any trouble before,

310
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:10,520
I hope you won't hold it against me.

311
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:12,120
-Happy birthday!
-Happy birthday!

312
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:13,520
-Thank you!
-Happy birthday!

313
00:19:20,840 --> 00:19:22,000
This second cup

314
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:23,840
is from my husband to all of you.

315
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:25,760
Grandmother's given her permission,

316
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:28,160
so he can set sail tomorrow!

317
00:19:28,240 --> 00:19:29,560
But he's only just recovered,

318
00:19:29,640 --> 00:19:31,760
so I'll drink for him.

319
00:19:31,840 --> 00:19:33,040
Cheers!

320
00:19:33,120 --> 00:19:34,920
-Congratulations, Yan!
-Congratulations!

321
00:19:39,480 --> 00:19:40,720
This third cup

322
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:42,360
is for some big news,

323
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:44,560
the most important news of all!

324
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:46,120
I, Jin Baozhu,

325
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:47,600
finally have my own salt shop!

326
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:49,680
-Congratulations!
-Congratulations!

327
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:52,440
Thank you!

328
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:54,240
Lady Jin's prepared a feast for us

329
00:19:54,320 --> 00:19:55,640
and bonus silver, too!

330
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:57,440
-Thank you, Lady Jin!
-Thank you, Lady Jin!

331
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:01,480
Eat, everyone! Eat!

332
00:20:02,280 --> 00:20:03,440
Here.

333
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:05,320
Here.

334
00:20:05,400 --> 00:20:06,480
Have some more.

335
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:13,760
-Heng,
-It's delicious! Delicious!

336
00:20:13,840 --> 00:20:14,880
a toast to you.

337
00:20:26,160 --> 00:20:27,200
If you can't manage the wine,

338
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:28,320
try some sour plum drink.

339
00:20:30,080 --> 00:20:32,000
-Thank you.
-It helps sober you up.

340
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:34,560
Jianwei,

341
00:20:35,480 --> 00:20:37,400
help Mr. Song back to rest.

342
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:39,480
-Yes.
-No need.

343
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:42,400
This sour plum drink has helped a lot.

344
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:43,560
Hasn't it?

345
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:45,320
Thank you for your concern.

346
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:47,880
Eat.

347
00:20:51,440 --> 00:20:54,600
Just eating and drinking is a little dull.

348
00:20:54,680 --> 00:20:55,720
Why don't we play a game?

349
00:20:57,040 --> 00:20:58,960
-What game?
-Pass the Flower.

350
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:00,360
Whoever's holding the flower

351
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:01,960
gives a line in Poetry Chain.

352
00:21:02,040 --> 00:21:03,640
-How's that?
-What's Poetry Chain?

353
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:07,240
We choose someone to act as caller,
who picks a word.

354
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:09,040
Then each of us recites a line of poetry

355
00:21:09,120 --> 00:21:11,160
containing that word.

356
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:12,360
If you can't answer,

357
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:14,320
you drink a cup of wine.

358
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:17,800
Why not just pour her a drink
and have her drink it?

359
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:19,680
-Why?
-You won't know a single line!

360
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:20,840
-Says who?
-She can be the caller.

361
00:21:20,920 --> 00:21:23,360
-Right!
-Even as caller, she'd get it wrong.

362
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:24,960
-Enough, enough.
-There's no way she can do it.

363
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:27,120
Let's begin. Use my flowers.

364
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:31,040
Then we'll use "pig,"
as in butchering pigs,

365
00:21:31,120 --> 00:21:32,160
for our word.

366
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:33,600
Yi, beat the drum!

367
00:21:49,320 --> 00:21:51,200
"At home, at this time of year,

368
00:21:51,280 --> 00:21:53,200
the wine is ripe, the pigs are fat."

369
00:21:56,840 --> 00:21:58,280
Good! Impressive!

370
00:22:15,560 --> 00:22:17,440
"A little pond to keep some cranes,

371
00:22:17,520 --> 00:22:19,680
and idle fields to graze the pigs."

372
00:22:20,520 --> 00:22:22,000
-Impressive!
-Good!

373
00:22:22,080 --> 00:22:23,200
-You're good!
-Very good!

374
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:41,320
"Tender pig's head, two fresh fish,

375
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:43,960
sweet bean paste and fragrant cakes."

376
00:22:44,040 --> 00:22:45,240
Good!

377
00:22:45,760 --> 00:22:47,040
That's good! Very good!

378
00:22:48,440 --> 00:22:50,400
-Well done!
-Impressive!

379
00:23:10,360 --> 00:23:12,040
Luck's not with me today,

380
00:23:12,120 --> 00:23:14,120
everyone, so I'll drink my penalty.

381
00:23:19,680 --> 00:23:22,200
-Not bad, right?
-Just a coincidence.

382
00:23:22,280 --> 00:23:24,720
-Don't blame me, Baozhu!
-Yan, a toast to you.

383
00:23:24,800 --> 00:23:26,160
All right. Thank you, Xi.

384
00:23:31,320 --> 00:23:33,720
You're quite the poet, Mr. Song.

385
00:23:33,800 --> 00:23:34,800
As are you.

386
00:23:42,280 --> 00:23:44,440
If you've had too much, why not go home?

387
00:23:46,880 --> 00:23:48,000
I'm fine.

388
00:23:48,720 --> 00:23:50,320
I'm usually alone,

389
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:52,000
but now,

390
00:23:52,480 --> 00:23:55,040
getting to sit with everyone
is really nice.

391
00:23:55,560 --> 00:23:57,040
You're not alone now.

392
00:23:57,120 --> 00:23:59,520
We're all here, aren't we?

393
00:24:01,960 --> 00:24:04,160
Eat. Have some food with your wine.

394
00:24:04,240 --> 00:24:05,640
-Have some food.
-Excuse me a moment.

395
00:24:09,760 --> 00:24:12,040
Yan, don't you believe me either?

396
00:24:13,720 --> 00:24:14,920
Give me the flowers.

397
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:17,080
Get him drunk again,
and you'll answer to me!

398
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:18,160
Have some more, then.

399
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:20,200
Here.

400
00:24:20,280 --> 00:24:21,520
Come on.

401
00:24:21,600 --> 00:24:22,760
Let's continue.

402
00:24:23,400 --> 00:24:24,840
-Here.
-Here.

403
00:24:41,360 --> 00:24:42,880
Quick, Yan!

404
00:24:43,840 --> 00:24:45,640
Don't tell me you can't think of a line!

405
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:47,280
Did you leave your brains at home?

406
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:49,000
I'll drink my penalty.

407
00:24:51,320 --> 00:24:52,680
He can't drink, so I'll drink for him.

408
00:24:53,320 --> 00:24:55,200
If I cheat over something so small,

409
00:24:55,280 --> 00:24:56,520
how will anyone trust me?

410
00:25:03,480 --> 00:25:04,600
"A black goat breaks the fence,

411
00:25:05,200 --> 00:25:06,720
a spotted pig bursts through the door."

412
00:25:07,960 --> 00:25:09,880
Young Master Xie,

413
00:25:09,960 --> 00:25:11,240
somehow that line just came to mind,

414
00:25:12,600 --> 00:25:13,640
so I thought I'd answer for you.

415
00:25:14,600 --> 00:25:15,640
Thank you.

416
00:25:17,440 --> 00:25:18,480
Thank you.

417
00:25:19,040 --> 00:25:21,360
Yi! Keep going!

418
00:25:33,800 --> 00:25:35,120
"A sharp blade cuts their heads off,

419
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:36,320
hung in rows like pigs and cattle."

420
00:25:37,120 --> 00:25:40,080
Mr. Song, a line came to me, too,

421
00:25:41,480 --> 00:25:42,840
so I thought I'd return the favor.

422
00:25:44,480 --> 00:25:45,600
Thank you.

423
00:25:47,960 --> 00:25:49,560
"They cook the pigs and kill the sheep,

424
00:25:49,640 --> 00:25:50,960
and boast it's sweet as honey."

425
00:25:51,040 --> 00:25:52,440
"Farmers don't send boys to herd pigs;

426
00:25:52,520 --> 00:25:54,360
an old crow tends the pigs instead."

427
00:25:54,440 --> 00:25:55,960
"By thirty, both are fully grown,

428
00:25:56,040 --> 00:25:57,200
one's a dragon, one's a pig."

429
00:25:57,280 --> 00:25:58,760
"Her brother heard that she was home,

430
00:25:58,840 --> 00:26:01,200
and sharpened knives for pigs and sheep."

431
00:26:01,280 --> 00:26:03,200
-Good lines! Good lines!
-You're too kind. Too kind.

432
00:26:04,880 --> 00:26:06,160
-Good!
-Good!

433
00:26:06,240 --> 00:26:07,920
-All good! All good!
-Yan's amazing! You're all amazing!

434
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:10,040
-Thank you.
-Simply amazing.

435
00:26:12,440 --> 00:26:14,960
At this hour,
why are they still making such a racket?

436
00:26:16,280 --> 00:26:17,680
-Have some food, everyone!
-Here!

437
00:26:17,760 --> 00:26:18,800
<i>Hanzhang! Hanzhang! I know it!</i>

438
00:26:18,880 --> 00:26:19,880
<i>I'll show you the moves.</i>

439
00:26:21,400 --> 00:26:23,840
<i>Lucky seven! Eight fine horses!</i>

440
00:26:23,920 --> 00:26:26,760
<i>Nine linked rings! Ten for all!</i>

441
00:26:26,840 --> 00:26:28,520
<i>Aren't you tired after all that shouting?</i>

442
00:26:28,600 --> 00:26:30,840
<i>-Sit down and eat something.</i>
<i>-Not tired!</i>

443
00:26:30,920 --> 00:26:32,160
<i>Here, here, here. Try this.</i>

444
00:26:35,840 --> 00:26:36,840
My lady.

445
00:26:37,640 --> 00:26:40,200
-My lady!
-Here, here. Fill it up!

446
00:26:40,280 --> 00:26:42,160
-Here! Here!
-Here!

447
00:26:42,240 --> 00:26:44,320
-Cheers!
-Let's go.

448
00:26:55,560 --> 00:26:59,640
I'll give the last line of the day.

449
00:27:00,960 --> 00:27:03,040
"With effort, hard things get done.

450
00:27:03,120 --> 00:27:05,040
With heat, a pig's head cooks through."

451
00:27:05,600 --> 00:27:08,600
Now, everyone go home and get some sleep!

452
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:11,040
Well said!

453
00:27:22,840 --> 00:27:23,920
Xie Yan!

454
00:27:24,480 --> 00:27:25,480
Let's go.

455
00:27:26,120 --> 00:27:27,280
Time to go home.

456
00:27:48,280 --> 00:27:49,800
Good boy!

457
00:27:49,880 --> 00:27:51,120
You've filled out!

458
00:27:51,200 --> 00:27:53,400
Where'd you put on all that muscle?

459
00:27:54,040 --> 00:27:55,720
I need to inspect you.

460
00:28:06,480 --> 00:28:08,760
Heaven help me!

461
00:28:08,840 --> 00:28:12,440
How can anyone be so handsome,

462
00:28:13,120 --> 00:28:14,760
so clever,

463
00:28:14,840 --> 00:28:16,680
and have so much money to spend?

464
00:28:20,160 --> 00:28:21,160
Xie Yan,

465
00:28:21,880 --> 00:28:24,200
are you happy today?

466
00:28:24,960 --> 00:28:28,080
I'm so happy!

467
00:28:31,120 --> 00:28:35,480
Since you're so good-looking,

468
00:28:36,720 --> 00:28:39,320
I'll tell you the truth.

469
00:28:40,600 --> 00:28:44,200
That day, when we talked things out,

470
00:28:45,080 --> 00:28:47,040
I was happy.

471
00:28:48,040 --> 00:28:50,160
But a little sad, too.

472
00:28:51,360 --> 00:28:53,160
Now your legs are better

473
00:28:53,240 --> 00:28:54,440
and Ms. Huang is gone,

474
00:28:54,520 --> 00:28:55,760
what if

475
00:28:55,840 --> 00:28:58,960
a Ms. Black or Ms. Green comes along?

476
00:28:59,040 --> 00:29:02,560
Let me tell you,
if you marry again, I'll hit--

477
00:29:03,640 --> 00:29:04,960
No!

478
00:29:05,040 --> 00:29:06,160
Forget I said that.

479
00:29:06,840 --> 00:29:09,600
Let's be practical.

480
00:29:09,680 --> 00:29:13,640
I want you to earn a lot of money

481
00:29:13,720 --> 00:29:15,880
so you can buy me

482
00:29:15,960 --> 00:29:17,840
agates the size of pigeon eggs

483
00:29:18,520 --> 00:29:20,560
and a butcher's knife of pure gold!

484
00:29:21,120 --> 00:29:24,320
And for every outfit,

485
00:29:24,400 --> 00:29:25,800
I want two of the same,

486
00:29:25,880 --> 00:29:26,880
so I can change between them.

487
00:29:27,440 --> 00:29:28,880
Agreed?

488
00:29:41,360 --> 00:29:44,800
Say nothing, and I'll take that as a yes.

489
00:29:58,320 --> 00:29:59,800
Xie Yan,

490
00:29:59,880 --> 00:30:01,560
I'm drunk.

491
00:30:03,560 --> 00:30:04,840
When someone's drunk,

492
00:30:05,520 --> 00:30:07,720
there's no telling what they might do.

493
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:09,680
Will you run?

494
00:30:11,440 --> 00:30:12,760
I'll count to ten.

495
00:30:13,760 --> 00:30:14,760
One.

496
00:30:16,360 --> 00:30:17,360
Two.

497
00:30:19,200 --> 00:30:20,200
Three.

498
00:30:21,600 --> 00:30:22,640
Ten!
